      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $9,$ the additive inverse of $-5$ modulo $9$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $-5$ modulo $9$ is the integer $0\\le x<9$ such that\n\n$$\nx+(-5)≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9).\n$$\n\nNotice that $5+(-5)≡0,$ so $x≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9),$ which is already in the required form. \n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $-5$ modulo $9$ is $5.$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
