      "dom_id": "question-213381",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $24,$ the additive inverse of $15$ modulo $24$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $15$ modulo $24$ is the integer $0\\le x<24$ such that\n\n$$\nx+15≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,24).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-15+15≡0,$ so $x≡-15\\,(\\text{mod}\\,24).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-15 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,24) \\\\  & ≡0-15 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,24) \\\\  & ≡24-15 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,24) \\\\  & ≡9 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,24)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $15$ modulo $24$ is $9.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n9+15≡24≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,24)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
