      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $33,$ the additive inverse of $17$ modulo $33$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $17$ modulo $33$ is the integer $0\\le x<33$ such that\n\n$$\nx+17≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,33).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-17+17≡0,$ so $x≡-17\\,(\\text{mod}\\,33).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-17 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,33) \\\\  & ≡0-17 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,33) \\\\  & ≡33-17 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,33) \\\\  & ≡16 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,33)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $17$ modulo $33$ is $16.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n16+17≡33≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,33)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
